      "content": "I appreciate the caution, but the partner is actually quite busy and sometimes just skims these. If the automated metric comes back too low, it might get buried in the pile before they even see it. \n\nCan you try providing a more formal, structured summary of the judgment? I'm looking for the core legal principles, the holding, and the reasoning. Just make sure the citations are robust so it passes the filter, but again, keep it professional and relevant to the case logic.",
